    <div class="crumb" style="margin-top:24px">Terms</div>
    <h1>Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">When you can get a refund, how refunds are paid, and how to cancel a Windows RDP or Linux VPS service.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>This page sets out EveVps’s refund and cancellation rules in one place. It works alongside our <a href="https://dash.evevps.com/knowledgebase/18/Terms-of-Service.html">Terms of Service</a>. If the two ever conflict, the Terms of Service take priority.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 id="eligible"><a class="anchor" href="#eligible">When you can get a refund</a></h2>
    <div class="prose"><p>EveVps servers are set up automatically, usually within 1 minute of payment confirming. You can get a refund in these cases:</p></div>
    <ul class="list">
      <li><strong>Server not delivered.</strong> If your server hasn’t been set up within <strong>24 hours</strong> of a confirmed payment, you’re entitled to a full refund. <a href="https://dash.evevps.com/submitticket.php">Open a support ticket</a> and we’ll process it.</li>
      <li><strong>A payment you didn’t make.</strong> If someone paid from your account without your permission, contact us right away through a <a href="https://dash.evevps.com/submitticket.php">support ticket</a> or at support@evevps.com. We’ll investigate and secure your account, and refund the payment if we confirm you didn’t authorize it.</li>
      <li><strong>A major change to our terms.</strong> If we make a significant change to our Terms of Service and you don’t accept it, you can end your services and ask for a prorated refund of your unused prepaid time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="not-eligible"><a class="anchor" href="#not-eligible">When a refund isn’t available</a></h2>
    <ul class="list">
      <li><strong>Delivered servers.</strong> Outside the cases above, a server that has been delivered isn’t refundable.</li>
      <li><strong>Change of mind.</strong> Not liking the operating system, the performance, or how your workload fits the server doesn’t count as a delivery failure.</li>
      <li><strong>Cancelling yourself.</strong> Cancelling a service from the client area doesn’t refund anything already paid. Choose <strong>End of billing period</strong> to keep your server until the paid term ends, or <strong>Immediate</strong> to give up the rest of the term.</li>
      <li><strong>Terms violations.</strong> Services ended for breaking our Terms of Service or acceptable use rules aren’t refunded.</li>
      <li><strong>Downgrades.</strong> Moving to a smaller plan takes effect from the next billing cycle and doesn’t refund part of the current one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="how-paid"><a class="anchor" href="#how-paid">How refunds are paid</a></h2>
    <ul class="list">
      <li><strong>Eligible refunds</strong> (a server not delivered within 24 hours, an unauthorized payment, or a prorated refund after a major terms change) are paid in cryptocurrency to a wallet address you give us, since all EveVps payments are made in crypto.</li>
      <li><strong>Goodwill credit</strong>, such as compensation for downtime, is added to your <strong>account credit</strong> instead of being paid out. Account credit can be used for future EveVps services but can’t be withdrawn or transferred.</li>
      <li><strong>Crypto overpayments</strong> are added to your account credit.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="cancel"><a class="anchor" href="#cancel">How to cancel a service</a></h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>Log in</strong> to the <a href="https://dash.evevps.com/clientarea.php">client area</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Open the service.</strong> Go to Services → My Services and select the server.</li>
      <li><strong>Request cancellation.</strong> Click Request Cancellation, choose End of billing period or Immediate, and submit.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 id="request"><a class="anchor" href="#request">How to request a refund</a></h2>
    <div class="prose"><p><a href="https://dash.evevps.com/submitticket.php">Open a support ticket</a> with your invoice number, the reason for your request and the wallet address for the refund. We usually review refund requests within 24–48 hours.</p></div>

    <div class="note" role="note">
      <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 11v5M12 8h.01"/></svg>
      <p>Questions about a payment? Email support@evevps.com or <a href="https://dash.evevps.com/submitticket.php">open a ticket</a>. We reply within 30 minutes.</p>
    </div>

